    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_art_primary_report_bug_description_a41402a1fbf0",
      "source_artifact_ref": "art_primary_report",
      "evidence_kind": "bug_description",
      "locator": {
        "locator_type": "line_range",
        "start_line": 18,
        "end_line": 26
      },
      "excerpt": "## Description\n\nWhen using torch.matmul with an out argument that is a view that is not contiguous, \nthe operation does not correctly write the result to the output tensor on the MPS backend.\n\nInstead of computing the matrix multiplication result, the output tensor remains unchanged\nand contains zeros.\n\n",
      "attribution": {
        "actor": null,
        "actor_role": "reporter"
      },
      "content_hash": "sha256:339552a4d00bd63b4b314e711c120003e29284d91b88fd09aefb30dec6be7d49"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_art_primary_report_observed_output_44989842eda4",
      "source_artifact_ref": "art_primary_report",
      "evidence_kind": "observed_output",
      "locator": {
        "locator_type": "line_range",
        "start_line": 55,
        "end_line": 68
      },
      "excerpt": "Observed Behavior\nOn MPS backend:\ntorch.matmul does not update the output tensor correctly.\nThe output remains zero.\nThe result differs from CPU implementation.\nThe issue may also cause segmentation faults in some cases,\nalthough the reporter could not provide a consistent reproduction.\nTrigger Conditions\nThe issue requires:\nAPI: torch.matmul\nBackend: MPS\nout argument is provided\nout tensor is a non-contiguous view\nsliced tensor view is used as output storage",
      "attribution": {
        "actor": null,
        "actor_role": "reporter"
      },
      "content_hash": "sha256:789987ed1cb510be6e8a6348497801a4372c650eb369db3706d7e0a87d848b4c"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_art_primary_report_api_reference_55e6e4494359",
      "source_artifact_ref": "art_primary_report",
      "evidence_kind": "api_reference",
      "locator": {
        "locator_type": "line_range",
        "start_line": 18,
        "end_line": 26
      },
      "excerpt": "## Description\n\nWhen using torch.matmul with an out argument that is a view that is not contiguous, \nthe operation does not correctly write the result to the output tensor on the MPS backend.\n\nInstead of computing the matrix multiplication result, the output tensor remains unchanged\nand contains zeros.\n\n",
      "attribution": {
        "actor": null,
        "actor_role": "reporter"
      },
      "content_hash": "sha256:339552a4d00bd63b4b314e711c120003e29284d91b88fd09aefb30dec6be7d49"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_art_primary_report_reproduction_c68f89f62c09",
      "source_artifact_ref": "art_primary_report",
      "evidence_kind": "reproduction",
      "locator": {
        "locator_type": "line_range",
        "start_line": 27,
        "end_line": 54
      },
      "excerpt": "## Minimal Reproduction\n\n```python\nimport torch\n\nX = torch.randn(256,256).to(\"mps\")\nY = torch.randn(256,256).to(\"mps\")\n\nZ = torch.zeros(256,2*256).to(\"mps\")\n\ntorch.matmul(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    out=Z[:,128:(128+256)]\n)\nThe same operation works correctly on CPU:\nimport torch\n\nX = torch.randn(256,256)\nY = torch.randn(256,256)\n\nZ = torch.zeros(256,2*256)\n\ntorch.matmul(\n    X,\n    Y,\n    out=Z[:,128:(128+256)]\n)",
      "attribution": {
        "actor": null,
        "actor_role": "reporter"
      },
      "content_hash": "sha256:28da3f523dba59231ed213e80436f1f59bd2ce8fe28f297fa48d6140d79942bd"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_art_primary_report_expected_behavior_56c8b3cb3189",
      "source_artifact_ref": "art_primary_report",
      "evidence_kind": "expected_behavior",
      "locator": {
        "locator_type": "line_range",
        "start_line": 72,
        "end_line": 74
      },
      "excerpt": "Expected Behavior\ntorch.matmul should correctly write the multiplication result into\nthe provided output tensor regardless of whether the output tensor is contiguous.",
      "attribution": {
        "actor": null,
        "actor_role": "reporter"
      },
      "content_hash": "sha256:4383ba00999d3b75f3d1a1f3e04e6003e72e65066e967f54c97b09ca4be4d28d"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_art_primary_report_environment_53986e744671",
      "source_artifact_ref": "art_primary_report",
      "evidence_kind": "environment",
      "locator": {
        "locator_type": "line_range",
        "start_line": 75,
        "end_line": 87
      },
      "excerpt": "Environment\nPyTorch version:\n2.0.1\nOS:\nmacOS 13.4\nDevice:\nApple M2 Max\nBackend:\nMPS\nIssue Status\nThe issue was triaged by PyTorch maintainers.\nLater discussion reported that the issue could no longer be reproduced\non newer nightly versions and a regression test was added.",
      "attribution": {
